1. Objective and execution instructions

Transform the existing SD OS Suite into a minimal, trustworthy, offline-first operations workspace. Preserve its useful core capabilities: auditing, operational metrics, reconciliation, analytics, workforce scheduling, tasks, employee performance scoring, directory, and spreadsheet exports. Add one application-wide conversational assistant that can query all available application data and execute supported application actions.

The core functionalities must be immediately visible. Remove simulated records, fake notifications, hardcoded metrics, canned findings, and unfinished controls masquerading as working features.

Work autonomously through implementation, testing, and fixes. Do not stop after planning, scaffolding, or one module. Make reasonable implementation decisions and document them. Do not ask for API keys, integrations, or routine design approvals. Optional providers will be configured later. Complete every core flow without external accounts. Respect repository instructions and preserve unrelated changes. Do not publish or deploy as part of this task.

