2. Architecture and scope

Retain a fully self-contained SD_OS_Suite.html build for offline use. Preserve useful vanilla JavaScript components and calculations where correct. Do not introduce React, a backend, cloud database, authentication platform, or deployment dependency merely for this redesign.

Organize source into clear modules for domain models, persistence, imports, calculations, application commands, selectors, UI components, and assistant tools. One centralized domain/service layer must power both UI and assistant actions. Avoid duplicate business logic in chat handlers. Use versioned schemas and runtime validation; use JSDoc or TypeScript where justified by the current build.

Use IndexedDB for durable structured datasets and localStorage only for small preferences where appropriate. All required scripts, fonts if any, and styles must be local or embedded. Opening the standalone HTML must not load remote assets. The included local-server mode must work too. Detect unavailable browser persistence and clearly explain session-only behavior without inventing successful saves. Browser/file-origin differences must be documented and tested where feasible.

Core operations require no LLM. Add a provider adapter for optional OpenAI-compatible tool-calling endpoints. An optional local relay may be provided if needed for server-side key handling or CORS; it must not become mandatory for core operations. Document localhost binding and allowed origins. Do not embed secrets or silently proxy through a third-party service.

