9. Verification and acceptance criteria

Replace misleading verification claims with measured results. Keep deterministic fixtures outside the production bundle. Add focused unit/integration tests for calculations and mutations, plus real browser tests for critical workflows; mocked DOM rendering alone is insufficient.

Required tests:

• Fresh startup has no fake people, tasks, tickets, audits, notifications, or calculated claims; all modules handle empty data.
• Real fixture imports validate, preserve provenance, reject invalid rows, and persist correctly after reload. Import replacement and restore are atomic.
• User changes across every module survive reload; complete backup/restore round-trips without credentials.
• SDR/cutoff/timezone boundaries, zero denominators, incomplete periods, missing inputs, and valid zero metrics behave correctly.
• Audits use exact evidence; unsupported criteria remain unassessed; security flags and review overrides are recorded accurately.
• Roster validation handles overnight rest, leave, custom policies, cross-week runs, infeasible demand, and stale draft application.
• Performance tests cover missing data, ties, weights, scoring bands, and reconciliation push previews.
• Assistant read tools agree with UI calculations; write tools use shared validation; retries do not duplicate mutations.
• Assistant tests cover ambiguous employee names, no-provider mode, provider failure, malformed tool calls, missing fields, blocked destructive writes, approval, undo, cancellation, and malicious instructions embedded in imported records.
• Real browser workflow: import team/tickets/demand → inspect metrics → run audit → create linked task → edit/validate roster → inspect performance → ask assistant a cross-module question → perform a task action → export → reload → verify results.
• Test at approximately 1440px, 1024px, 768px, and 390px; verify keyboard flows, dialogs, drawer focus, table scrolling, readable themes, and no console errors in completed flows.
• Verify assembled standalone output and local-server mode. Check there are no automatic network requests in offline mode and no demo data bundled into production.

Use test provider doubles only in tests. If no real provider credentials are available, complete and test the provider contract and failure states, but explicitly report live-provider verification as Not run. Do not claim production-ready, benchmark passed, fully tested, or optimized without corresponding evidence.

